From d9ec151d65fc0bd99fc9265f183cf3d057cdec68 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 06:19:11 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Location of the arrays of a material data manager

The location of the arrays (MemoryLocation: host, device or shared) is a
property of the data, declared by the initializer of a material data
manager and checked:

- a behaviour generated by the generic-parallel interface with the cuda or
  hip backend refuses data located in the memory of the host;
- when the arrays are not located in the memory of the host, all the arrays
  of the states must be given by the initializer, and the arrays of the
  tangent operators and of the speed of sound must be given if they are
  used: the arrays allocated by the manager are in the memory of the host;
- update and revert, which copy the states on the host, refuse data located
  in the memory of a device.

The headers BatchExecutionPolicy.hxx and MemoryLocation.hxx are installed
(the first one was missing).

GenericParallelCUDATest declares the managed memory as shared and checks
each refusal by its message.
